  "authoringNote": "Snapshot only (D4 contrast to F10x1). f10x2-supplier-status v1 fails provenance: its contentHash is the SHA-256 of alternate bytes (the same body with effectiveTo 2026-06-29), and its held body states an expired interval 2025-07-01 to 2026-06-30. It supplies no fact. v2 of the same ID is available, hash-matching and states SYN-SUP-0001, non_exempt, established, no new enrollment or ownership change and 2026-02-01 to 2027-01-31, equal to the case. Its supersedes is null, and C08 infers no relationship from the larger version number, so this vector holds two current versions and no supersession edge; both lists are empty. A current usable supplier record named by supplierStatusEvidenceId exists, so the failed-provenance qualifier of R01 does not hold: R01 passes with no condition and an empty parent, citing the seven v2 supplier fields and the order /item/code (8). No v1 value is cited or compared. R09 still classifies v1: conflict for the administrative_reviewer with R09.hash_mismatch naming f10x2-supplier-status v1 (needs_human_review), parent [f10x2-supplier-status v1]. The usable v2 does not cure the v1 provenance failure. State needs_human_review. R02 to R05 pass with the standard citation sets (6, 9, 6, 4). R06 is manual_review for the qualified_clinical_reviewer with R06.clinical_review (no refs, effect none) and cites the five /clinical/ statements of the usable encounter; R07 passes citing /lcmpReport/incorporated (false; the null evaluationDate is not cited); R08 passes; R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. Every other parent is empty. Recorded reading: a rule cites evidence-field facts only from the documents it reads, and R04 reads only final current usable records; every usable encounter and order here is final, so no draft is excluded. The standard chronology holds: the order date 2026-09-08 is after the 2026-08-24 encounter (not the same day, so C02 does not apply) and inside the C01 bound 2027-02-24, and the receipt at 2026-09-09T16:30:00Z is after the C06 span of the order date, which ends 2026-09-09T12:00Z. Deferred to S4: replacing the failed record in a later snapshot and the reassessment it triggers are not exercised; no applied supersession relation is claimed.",
